hadiths[65]{hadithnumber,text}:
"591","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""When a woman separates herself from her husband's bed, the angels continue to curse her until she returns."
"592","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you calls his wife to bed and she refuses, and he spends the night angry with her, then the angels continue to curse her until morning."
"593","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Do not secretly kill your children, for «غيلة» (having intercourse with a nursing woman) even affects a horseman and causes him to fall from his horse."
"594","Amr bin Maymun bin Mehran narrated from his father: He said: Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah was married to Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him). He went out for prayer, and she began experiencing labor pains and concealed it. She said: “Make my heart happy by giving me one divorce.” So he gave her one divorce. When he returned (after praying), she had given birth to the child. So he went to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and asked him about the matter. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “According to Allah’s law, the prescribed period has been completed; send her a marriage proposal.” He said: “She deceived me, may Allah deceive her.”"
"595","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever has two wives and inclines towards one of them, neglecting the other, will come on the Day of Resurrection with one side of his body fallen."
"596","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If it were not for the Children of Israel, meat would not decay (become foul), nor would food spoil, and if it were not for Hawwa (Eve), a woman would not be unfaithful (deceitful) to her husband."
"597","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A woman should not lie down with a woman, a man should not lie down with a man, and a child should not lie down with a child, with their bodies touching."
"598","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns a servant against his people (master), he is not from among us, and whoever turns a woman against her husband, then he is not from among us."
"599","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a woman be married to a man who already has her paternal aunt in his wedlock, and (likewise) that a paternal aunt be married to a man who already has her niece in his wedlock."
"600","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a woman be married to a man who already has her paternal aunt in his wedlock, and likewise, that a woman be married to a man who already has her niece in his wedlock. And a woman should not be married to a man who already has her maternal aunt in his wedlock, nor should a maternal aunt be married to a man who already has her niece in his wedlock. And the younger should not be married while the elder is present, nor should the elder be married while the younger is present."
"601","Hazrat Aamir narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"602","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every sermon in which the testimony (of the Oneness of Allah and the Messengership) is not mentioned is like a severed hand."
"603","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no Shighar (a type of marriage) in Islam."" And that is when a woman is married in exchange for the dowry of another woman, he says: Marry her to me and I will marry her to you, and there will be no dowry; this is called Shighar."
"604","With the same (previous) chain of narration: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept it; then he should either eat or (pray) for the household. If the messenger enters before him, then that is his permission, and if he enters before him, then he should seek permission."
"605","Sayyida Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me on the day of my marriage and sat down at my bedding place, while two girls were with me beating the duff and mentioning in their poetry my forefathers who were martyred at the Battle of Badr. They also said in their verses: “Among us is a Prophet who knows what will happen today and tomorrow.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “As for this statement, do not say it.”"
"606","Ibrahim bin Maisarah narrated: His maternal aunt narrated from a woman, who is trustworthy, that the woman said: My father was in a battle during the days of ignorance, and due to the heat, his feet began to burn. A man said: Whoever gives me his shoes, I will marry my first-born daughter to him. So my father took off his shoes and threw them towards him. That man had a daughter born to him, and when she reached maturity, my father said: Gather my family to me, and said: Bring me the dowry. My father said: By Allah! I will not add anything to what I gave you for the two shoes. He said: By Allah! I will give her to you in exchange for the dowry. So my father went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked him about it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you something better than that? Leave her, and do not become sinful by breaking your oath, and your companion will not be sinful either."" So my father left her."
"607","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar that Habibah bint Sahal (may Allah be pleased with her) was the wife of Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him). He beat her severely, so she came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this to him and said: ""It is impossible for me and Thabit to live together."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Thabit! Take (the dowry) from her."" He said: ""What I gave her is exactly with me."" So it was taken from her (Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her), and she observed her waiting period ('iddah) at her family's house."
"608","Lady Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by us while we were sitting among women. He greeted us with peace, then said: “Beware of «منعمين» (those who do good, husbands) and do not be ungrateful to them.” We asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by being ungrateful to «منعمين» ? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It may be that one of you is with her parents before marriage, then Allah grants her a husband and blesses her with wealth and children through him, but then (the woman), in anger, says: I have never seen any good from you.”"
"609","Lady Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by us while we were among the women, and he greeted us with salam. Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We replied to your salam. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of being ungrateful for «منعمين» ."" Then the narrator mentioned the hadith similar to the previous one, and said: ""So you, in anger, swear by Allah and say, 'I have never seen any good from you.'"
"610","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by us while we were girls of the same age, and he said: “Avoid being ungrateful for «منعمين» .” We asked: What is meant by being ungrateful for «منعمين» ? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It may be that one of you remains unmarried for a long time until she grows old without marriage, then Allah grants her a husband and children, and then in a fit of anger she says: I have never seen any good from you.”"
"611","Sayyiduna Abu Sanabil (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Sabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) gave birth to a child twenty or thirty days after her husband’s death. When she became pure from postnatal bleeding, she expressed her intention to marry, so this matter was considered objectionable in her case. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: “When her waiting period has ended, then what is there to prevent her (from marrying)?”"
"612","Shu’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) gave a fatwa regarding a woman whose husband passes away, so they sent a message to Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked her about this matter. She said: Subai’ah gave birth to a child about a month after her husband’s death. So when she gave birth and became pure (from postpartum bleeding), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: “You may marry whomever you wish.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say: Complete whichever of the two periods is longer."
"613","Yahya ibn Hammad informed us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Al-Aswad, from Abu Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, the like of it."
"614","It is narrated from Masruq and Ibn Utbah that both of them wrote a letter to Sabi’ah bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked her about her situation: so she wrote them a reply that she had given birth to a child twenty-five days after the death of her husband, so she intended to seek goodness (marriage), then Abu Sanabil (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by her and said to her: You have acted hastily, complete the last of the two waiting periods, and that is four months and ten days. So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray for forgiveness for me. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For what reason?” She said: I told you the incident. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “If you find a righteous man, then marry.”"
"615","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah that Abdullah bin Utbah wrote a letter to Abdullah bin Arqam, asking him to go to Sabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) and inquire from her about the fatwa that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had given her. She had given birth to a child just a few days later. When she gave birth to the child, she adorned herself. Abu As-Sanabil (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by her and said to her: “Perhaps you wish to get married. By Allah! No, not until four months and ten days have passed since your husband’s death.” So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this to him, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: “You have completed your waiting period (‘iddah).”"
"616","Abu Salamah narrated: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) were asked about a woman whose husband passes away and she gives birth to a child before four months and ten days. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: She should complete whichever of the two periods is longer. Abu Salamah narrated: When she gives birth to the child, her waiting period is completed. Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I am with my nephew Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman (in his opinion). So they sent a message to Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) while she was in her chamber in the mosque. They asked her about this matter, and she said: Sabi’ah bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) gave birth to a child just a few days after her husband’s death. When she was purified from postpartum bleeding, she wore good clothes and applied kohl. Abu Sanabil (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by her and said to her: Do you wish to marry? (Marriage) is not (permissible) until you complete four months and ten days. So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this to him, and he commanded her to marry."
"617","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah that Marwan bin Hakam sent Abdullah bin Utbah to Sabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) so that he could inquire from her about her issue. She mentioned it in the same way as Abu Salamah had described in her case. Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Her husband was Sa’d bin Khawlah (may Allah be pleased with him), who passed away in the year of the conquest of Makkah. He had participated in the Battle of Badr."
"618","Lady Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The example of a woman who adorns herself for others besides her family is like darkness on the Day of Resurrection; there will be no light for her."
"619","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""No woman should mourn for anyone who has died for more than three days except for her husband, for she should mourn for him for four months and ten days. She should not apply kohl, nor wear colored clothes, but she may wear some white and some colored clothes, and she should not use perfume except after completing her menstruation, at the time of bathing, she may use a little bit of Indian aloeswood and azfar (a type of perfume)."
"620","Hisham narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"621","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We were commanded not to wear colored clothes during mourning for a husband, except for a garment that was partly white and partly colored."
"622","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We were commanded not to apply perfume during mourning, except that after purification from menstruation, we may use a little bit of Indian aloeswood and azfar perfume at the time of bathing."
"623","Lady Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: My husband divorced me three times during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he did not assign me any residence or maintenance. Mughira narrated: I came to Ibrahim and mentioned this to him, and he said: She is entitled to residence and maintenance. I mentioned to him the statement of Shabi, and he said: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to assign this (residence and maintenance) for the divorced woman. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Because of the statement of one woman, we cannot leave the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him); who knows, perhaps she remembered or perhaps she forgot."
"624","It is narrated from Sayyida Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) that she was divorced during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not assign her any residence or maintenance. And that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""We cannot abandon the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) because of what a woman says; I do not know, perhaps she has forgotten."
"625","Shu'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: Sayyida Fatima bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him that her husband gave her three divorces and she spent her waiting period ('iddah) at the house of her paternal cousin, Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"626","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: My husband gave me three divorces. I went to his agent to ask him for maintenance, but he said: ""You are entitled to neither residence nor maintenance."" So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this to him, and he (peace be upon him) said: ""He has spoken the truth."
"627","It is narrated from Sayyida Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her): She presented herself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he did not assign her any residence nor maintenance."
"628","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My husband gave me three divorces, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not prescribe for me either accommodation or maintenance."
"629","Abu Salamah narrated from Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her): She said: I wrote the book by listening from her mouth."
"630","Lady Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I was the wife of a man from the Banu Makhzum tribe, and he gave me an irrevocable divorce. I sent a message to his family and demanded maintenance from them, but they said: “You have no maintenance due from us.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There is no maintenance due to you from them, and you must observe the waiting period (‘iddah). Go to the house of Umm Sharik, and do not neglect to inform us when you make a decision regarding yourself.” Then he said: “At Umm Sharik’s house, the early emigrant Muslim brothers come and go. Go to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; even if you take off your clothes, he will not see anything of you. And do not neglect to inform us when you make a decision regarding yourself.” She (Fatimah bint Qais, may Allah be pleased with her) said: Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm al-Adawi (may Allah be pleased with them) both sent me marriage proposals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “As for Muawiyah, he is a poor man and has nothing. As for Abu Jahm, he never puts his stick down from his shoulder (he is harsh-tempered). What do you think about Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him)?” Her family did not like him, but she said: “I will marry the one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has invited me.” So I married Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"631","Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated that Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Fatimah! Fear Allah, you know what its outcome will be."
"632","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said regarding Allah Almighty’s statement: « لَا تُخْرِجُوهُنَّ مِن بُيُوتِهِنَّ وَلَا يَخْرُجْنَ إِلَّا أَن يَأْتِينَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ » “Do not drive them out of their houses, nor should they leave, unless they commit a clear indecency.” In its explanation, he said: « وَالْفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ » This means that she becomes a cause of disgrace for her family, so when she does this, it becomes lawful for them to expel her."
"633","Muhammad bin Amr narrated with this chain in a similar manner (as the previous hadith)."
"634","Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her), the sister of Dhahhak bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him), narrated: She was the wife of a man from the Banu Makhzum tribe. He gave her three divorces and himself went out on a military expedition, and he told his agent to give her some maintenance. So I considered it insufficient, and I went to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came while she was with her. She said: O Messenger of Allah! This is Fatimah bint Qais. So-and-so has given her three divorces, and he has ordered a small amount of maintenance for her, but she did not accept it, and he said that even this is a favor upon her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He has spoken the truth."" And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: ""Go to Umm Maktum and spend your waiting period with her."" Then he said: ""She is a woman with many visitors. Go to Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum and spend your waiting period with him."" So I went to Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum and spent my waiting period with him. When my waiting period ended, Abu Jahm bin Hudhayfah and Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both) sent me proposals of marriage. I consulted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for Abu Jahm bin Hudhayfah, he is a man who carries a stick, so you may fear being beaten, and as for Muawiyah, he is poor and has no wealth."" So Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) married her."
"635","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah that Abu Amr bin Hafs bin Mughira set out towards Yemen with Ali bin Abi Talib, so he sent the final divorce to Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) and told Harith bin Hisham and Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah to give her maintenance. So both of them said to her: By Allah! You are not entitled to maintenance unless you are pregnant. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this to him, so he (peace be upon him) said: “There is no maintenance for you, so spend your waiting period (‘iddah) at the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, as he is blind. You may even remove your clothes in his presence, and he will not be able to see you.” So when she completed her ‘iddah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married her to Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him). The news of this reached Marwan, so he sent Qabeesah bin Dhuwayb to her to ask her about this hadith, and she narrated it to him. So Marwan said: This hadith has only been heard from one woman; we will only follow the path upon which we found the people. When Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) heard Marwan’s statement, she said: Between me and you is the Qur’an (as evidence). Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has said in His Book: “They should not leave (their houses) unless they commit a clear/manifest indecency.” Perhaps after that Allah will bring about some (other) way. So it was said: This is for the one who has the right to take her back; after three divorces, what way will be brought about? He is not obliged to spend on you unless you are pregnant, so on what basis will they prevent her?"
"636","Maymun bin Mehran narrated: I asked Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, about a woman divorced thrice: where should she observe her waiting period ('iddah)? He said: In her husband's house. So I said to him: What about the hadith of Fatimah bint Qais, may Allah be pleased with her? He said: That woman has put people to trial; she was ill-mannered, or he said: She was a woman who did not treat her husband's relatives well."
"637","Maimun bin Mehran narrated: I mentioned to Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) the hadith of Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her), so he said: This woman has put people to trial."
"638","Maimun bin Mehran narrated: I came to Madinah Munawwarah and inquired about the greatest jurist there, so I was sent to Saeed bin Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him. I asked him about a woman who has been given three divorces: where should she spend her waiting period (‘iddah)? He said: In her husband's house. I said: Fatimah bint Qais, the sister of Dhahhak bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him), was given three divorces by her husband, so she spent her ‘iddah at the house of Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him). He replied: That woman had bad manners, so she was made to stay at the house of Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"639","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man (Salamah bin Sakhr) pronounced zihar upon his wife (said to her: ""You are to me like the back of my mother""), then he saw her in the moonlight, she pleased him, so he had intercourse with her. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, not say: 'Before they touch each other'?"" He replied: ""I saw her and she pleased me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Refrain until you have offered the expiation."
"640","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Sakhr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I made zihar from my wife, then I had intercourse with her. So I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered me: ""Feed sixty needy people."
"641","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: During the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and for two years of the leadership/caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), three divorces were counted as only one divorce. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You were commanded to be patient and forbearing regarding divorce, but you hastened in your forbearance, so we have enforced your hastiness upon you."
"642","It is narrated from Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abu As-Sahba said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): Present something from your words—were not three divorces counted as one during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)? The matter was like that. When the era of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came, people began to give divorce without thinking, so he enforced it upon them."
"643","It is narrated from Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abu As-Sahba said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): ""Do you not know that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and for three years of the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), three divorces were counted as only one?"" So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""Yes."
"644","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""If a husband has not had relations with his wife and gives her three divorces at once, then they will take effect upon her."
"645","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I mentioned this to Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him), so he said: I testify that I heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) considering them as one. The narrator stated, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It is only one, even if he combined them."
"646","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: Whether marital relations have been established with a woman or not, in the matter of three divorces, they are equal."
"647","Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: One of my ancestors gave his wife a thousand divorces, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) enforced it. And he said: ""Your father did not adopt piety, so he did not make any way out for him. Three of them have been enforced on his behalf, and the rest are excess; he has made a mockery of the verses of Allah."
"648","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The best among your women is the one whose dowry is the easiest among you."" Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) used to say: Even if it is one dirham, it is lawful."
"649","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: We participated with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) in the funeral of the noble wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Maymunah, at the place of Saraf. He said: This is the noble wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so when you lift her body, do not shake it, do not jolt it, and be gentle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had nine pure wives; he had assigned turns for eight of them, but had not assigned a turn for one. Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) said: We found out that the one for whom the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had not assigned a turn was Lady Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"650","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned his daughter Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) to her husband Abu Al-As bin Al-Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) with the first marriage after two years."
"651","Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated with this chain the same narration, and he transmitted this addition: He said, ""No new act was done (i.e., neither a new marriage nor a new dowry, etc.), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had already kept her with him before this."
"652","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Qutaylah, the sister of Ash'ath bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him), but he passed away before consummating the marriage with her, so Allah absolved him of her."
"653","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when Ma'iz (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he had committed adultery, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""Perhaps you only touched, or looked, or kissed."" The narrator stated that it was as if the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) feared that he might not know what adultery actually is."
"654","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): A woman got married during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and she had accepted Islam. Then her (first) husband came and said: I had accepted Islam along with her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) separated her from her later husband and returned her to her first husband."
"655","Israel (bin Yunus bin Abi Ishaq), may Allah have mercy on him, narrated from this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
